#!/bin/bash
# Omarchy's SUPER+K, ported. A static sheet.
#
# It used to parse ~/.aerospace.toml so it could not drift. AeroSpace is gone
# and there is no longer a single file that holds the whole keymap: the app
# keys are Karabiner's, window management and the rest are Raycast's and live
# in Raycast's own database. So this is maintained by hand -- if you change a
# binding, change it here too.
#
# Install: Raycast › Extensions › Script Commands › Add Directories
#          -> point at this folder. Then give it hotkey Caps + K.
#
# @raycast.schemaVersion 1
# @raycast.title Keybindings
# @raycast.mode fullOutput
# @raycast.packageName Omakase
# @raycast.icon ⌨️

cat <<'EOF'

  SUPER = Caps Lock (⌘⌃⌥).  Tap Caps alone for Escape.

  WINDOWS — Raycast Window Management, fractional (adapts to the screen
  you're on). Bound in Raycast's own UI; these are NOT in the dotfiles repo.
    SUPER+←  /  SUPER+→        Left half / right half
    SUPER+↑  /  SUPER+↓        Top half / bottom half
    SUPER+SHIFT+←  /  +→       Move to previous / next display
    SUPER+F                    Maximize
    SUPER+C                    Center
    SUPER+R                    Restore
    drag to a screen edge      macOS native tiling, still on (incl. top edge)

  RAYCAST
    SUPER+SPACE                Command menu
    SUPER+SHIFT+SPACE          App search
    SUPER+V                    Clipboard history
    SUPER+K                    This sheet
    SUPER+S                    Capture
    SUPER+X                    Extract text (OCR)
    SUPER+P                    Colour picker
    SUPER+ESC                  System menu

  MACOS NATIVE
    ⌘C / ⌘V / ⌘X               Copy / paste / cut, everywhere including terminals
    ⌘TAB                       Cycle apps
    ⌃⌘SPACE                    Emoji picker
    ⌃←  /  ⌃→                  Previous / next Space

EOF
